// ==============================================
// RECURSIVE RELATIONSHIP (1 Required) - ENHANCED
// ==============================================

// User Self-Referencing: Host-Guest Dual Role (ENHANCED)
// Users can act as both hosts and guests through the booking ecosystem
// Implementation: Users reference other users through:
// - As hosts: via properties.host_id → host_profiles.host_profile_id → users.user_id
// - As guests: via bookings.guest_profile_id → guest_profiles.guest_profile_id → users.user_id
// - Connection: When a guest books a property, they create a relationship with the host user
// Cardinality: (0,N) ↔ (0,N)
// A user can host for N other users (through property bookings)
// A user can be a guest of N other users (by booking their properties)
// The same user account can simultaneously act as both host AND guest

// This recursive relationship is implemented through the booking system:
// - properties.host_id → host_profiles.host_profile_id → users.user_id (user as host)
// - bookings.guest_profile_id → guest_profiles.guest_profile_id → users.user_id (user as guest)
// - When guest books host's property, connection is established
// - Users can book other users' properties while also hosting their own

// ==============================================
// BUSINESS RULES IMPLEMENTATION (ENHANCED)
// ==============================================

// Data Integrity Rules (ENHANCED)
// - All foreign keys must reference existing records
// - Email addresses must be unique across all users
// - Phone numbers must be unique and valid format
// - Booking dates must be valid and non-overlapping
// - Payment amounts must be positive
// - Guest profiles created automatically on first booking
// - Host profiles created when user applies to become host
// - Role flags must be consistent with profile existence
// - All URLs must follow proper format validation
// - All monetary amounts must be positive
// - All ratings must be within valid ranges (1-5)
// - All percentages must be between 0-100

// Business Logic Rules (ENHANCED)
// - Users must verify identity before listing properties
// - Bookings cannot be made for past dates
// - Reviews can only be written after stay completion
// - Payments must be processed before check-in
// - Hosts receive payouts 24 hours after guest check-in
// - Users can hold multiple roles simultaneously
// - Property ownership explicitly tied to host_profiles
// - Booking actions explicitly tied to guest_profiles
// - All verification statuses must follow defined workflows
// - All payment methods must be valid and active

// Security Rules (ENHANCED)
// - Passwords must be hashed and never stored in plain text
// - Payment information must be encrypted
// - Personal data must be protected according to privacy laws
// - Access control based on user roles and permissions
// - Tax information in host_profiles must be encrypted
// - All sensitive data must follow encryption standards
// - Audit trails maintained for all financial transactions

